    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1.84$ seconds.",
      "worked": "Substitute $h=27$.\n$$\\begin{align*}27&=23.7t-4.9t^2\\\\4.9t^2-23.7t+27&=0\\\\49t^2-237t+270&=0\\\\(49t-90)(t-3)&=0\\\\t&=\\frac{90}{49}\\text{ or }3\\end{align*}$$\nThe arrow first reaches $27$ metres on its way up, at $t=\\frac{90}{49}\\approx1.84$ seconds. It reaches that height again on its way down at $3$ seconds.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
